@*
    What a block states that the devbook convention reports, listed under the
    headline of the record it is about.

    Under the headline and above the fields, because a finding is about the block
    as a whole and is the thing an author has to act on; below the fields it would
    read as one more field. Compact on purpose — one line each, the severity, the
    field it names and one sentence — because a record is secondary to the chapter
    it sits over, and a finding is secondary to the record.

    A list, not an alert. Nothing here happened just now: a finding is a standing
    property of the text, so it is announced the way the rest of the record is,
    when a reader reaches it, rather than interrupting them with role="alert" on
    every render of every chapter.

    The severity is a Badge in a `finding` family, and it is a word as well as a
    tone — "warning", "error" — so the colour never carries the meaning on its own.
    The field is drawn through MetadataScalar, the same code span a field's value
    wears, because it is a key an author will go looking for in the fence.

    Empty in, nothing out.
*@

@if (Findings.Count > 0)
{
    <ul class="devbook-findings" aria-label="Metadata findings" data-testid="@TestId">@foreach (var finding in Findings)
        {
            <li class="@ItemClass(finding)"><Badge Kind="finding" Slug="@Slug(finding)">@Slug(finding)</Badge><MetadataScalar Value="@finding.Field" /><span class="devbook-findings__message">@finding.Message</span></li>
        }</ul>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>The findings, in the order <see cref="DevbookMetadataFindings"/>
    /// produced them.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<DevbookMetadataFinding> Findings { get; set; } = [];

    [Parameter]
    public string? TestId { get; set; } = "devbook-findings";

    private static string Slug(DevbookMetadataFinding finding) =>
        finding.Severity == DevbookFindingSeverity.Error ? "error" : "warning";

    private static string ItemClass(DevbookMetadataFinding finding) =>
        $"devbook-findings__item devbook-findings__item--{Slug(finding)}";
}
